NAME
    dep - deposit bytes into memory

SYNOPSIS
    dep addr byte [byte ...]

DESCRIPTION
    Stores one or more hexadecimal byte values into memory starting at
    the hexadecimal address addr. The counterpart to dump. Quiet on
    success. dep is a /bin program (formerly an OS built-in).

NOTES
    dep writes anywhere in the 64K space, including over the resident OS.
    Because it loads into the TPA at $6A00, depositing into its own
    footprint (roughly $6A00..$7A00) corrupts the running program -- so
    dep into other regions (OS variables, high RAM, the I/O ports).

EXAMPLES
    dep 9000 41 42 43     store "ABC" at $9000
    dep FF02 AA           drive the LED port

SEE ALSO
    dump, save, load
